Mini Project — Deploy NGINX Server on AWS EC2
Ab hum complete practical karain gay step by step.
Project Goal:
•	EC2 server launch
•	NGINX install
•	Port 80 open
•	HTML page deploy
•	Browser mn website open
Tum already PuTTY mn ho, to ab directly server py kaam karte hain.
STEP 1 — Check Current User
PuTTY mn command run karo:
whoami
Agar ubuntu ya root aa raha hai to perfect.
STEP 2 — Update Server
sudo apt update -y
Purpose:
•	Linux packages latest karta hai.
STEP 3 — Install NGINX
sudo apt install nginx -y
STEP 4 — Check NGINX Status
sudo systemctl status nginx
Agar green active (running) aa raha hai to nginx chal gaya.
Exit karne ke liye:
q
________________________________________
STEP 5 — Enable NGINX
Ye reboot ke baad bhi nginx automatically start karega.
sudo systemctl enable nginx
STEP 6 — Open Port 80 in AWS
Ab browser side ka kaam.
AWS Console kholo:
EC2 → Instances → Apna Instance → Security
Phir:
Security Groups → Edit inbound rules
Add Rule:
Type	Port	Source
HTTP	80	Anywhere IPv4
Save Rules.
STEP 7 — Check Website
Browser mn ye open karo:
http://YOUR-PUBLIC-IP
Example:
http://13.232.xx.xx
Agar "Welcome to nginx!" aa gaya to server successfully chal gaya 🎉
STEP 8 — Deploy Custom HTML Page
Ab default nginx page remove karte hain.
NGINX default folder:
/var/www/html
Us folder mn jao:
cd /var/www/html
STEP 9 — Check Existing Files
ls
Tumhe mostly:
index.nginx-debian.html
dikhegi.
STEP 10 — Remove Default Page
sudo rm index.nginx-debian.html
STEP 11 — Create New HTML Page
sudo nano index.html
Ab ye HTML paste karo:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>My DevOps Project</title>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Welcome To My NGINX Server</h1>
    <h2>Mini DevOps Project Successfully Deployed</h2>

    <p>This website is hosted on AWS EC2 using NGINX.</p>

</body>
</html>
STEP 12 — Save File
Nano editor mn:
Press:
CTRL + O
Enter press karo.
Phir:
CTRL + X
STEP 13 — Restart NGINX
sudo systemctl restart nginx
STEP 14 — Open Website Again
Browser mn:
http://YOUR-PUBLIC-IP
Ab tumhari custom HTML website show hogi 🎉
